  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>Members of a high school math club have a scavenger hunt. Three items are hidden in the
        park, which is a rectangle that measures 50 meters by 20 meters.</para>
      <list>
        <item>The clues are written as systems of inequalities. One system has no solutions.</item>
        <item>The locations of the items can be narrowed down by solving the systems. A coordinate
          plane can be used to describe the solutions.</item>
      </list>
      <!--Q#1-->

      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Can you find the hidden items? Sketch a graph to show where each item could be
            hidden.</para>
          <para>You will be provided with a sheet of graph paper to help solve this scavenger hunt
            without the use of technology. For each clue, graph each inequality separately on the
            same coordinate grid.  </para>
          <para>
            <emphasis>Clue 1:</emphasis>
          </para>
          <para>\(y&gt;14\)\(x&lt;10\)</para>
     
            <figure class="unnumbered">
              <media
                alt="Blank grid, origin O. X axis, scale is 0 to 40, by 10’s. Y axis, scale is 0 to 20, by 10’s.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_01.svg" />
              </media>
            
     
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="Graph of 2 intersecting inequalities. Horizontal axis, labeled x, from 0 to 50 by 5s. Vertical axis, labeled y, from 0 to 30 by 5s. Shading to left of vertical line. Shading above horizontal line.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_02.svg" />
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#2-->

      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>
            <emphasis>Clue 2:</emphasis>
          </para>
          <para>\(x+y&lt;20\)\(x&gt;6\)</para>
          <para>
            <figure class="unnumbered">
              <media
                alt="Blank grid, origin O. X axis, scale is 0 to 40, by 10’s. Y axis, scale is 0 to 20, by 10’s.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_03.svg" />
              </media>
            
          </para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="Graph of 2 intersecting inequalities. Horizontal axis, labeled x, from 0 to 50 by 5s. Vertical axis, labeled y, from 0 to 30 by 5s. Shading to right of vertical line. Shading below slanted line.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_04.svg" />
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#3-->

      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>
            <emphasis>Clue 3:</emphasis>
          </para>
          <para>\(y&lt;-2x+20\)\(y&lt;-2x+10\)</para>
          <para>
            <figure class="unnumbered">
              <media
                alt="Blank grid, origin O. X axis, scale is 0 to 40, by 10’s. Y axis, scale is 0 to 20, by 10’s.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_05.svg" />
              </media>
            
          </para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="Graph of 2 inequalities. Horizontal axis, labeled x, from 0 to 50 by 5s. Vertical axis, labeled y, from 0 to 30 by 5s. Lines parallel. Shading below each line.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_06.svg" />
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#4-->

      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>
            <emphasis>Clue 4:</emphasis>
          </para>
          <para>\(y\geq x+10\)\(x&gt;y\)</para>
          <para>
            <figure class="unnumbered">
              <media
                alt="Blank grid, origin O. X axis, scale is 0 to 40, by 10’s. Y axis, scale is 0 to 20, by 10’s.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_07.svg" />
              </media>
            
          </para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="Graph of 2 inequalities that don’t intersect. Horizontal axis, labeled x, from 0 to 50 by 5s. Vertical axis, labeled y, from 0 to 30 by 5s. Lines parallel. Shading below dotted line, above solid line.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_09_08.svg" />
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#5-->

      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Reflect: When you graphed each pair of inequalities, you created a system of
            inequalities. Where did the possible solutions lie on the graph?</para>
          <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to
            compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Solution Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. Where the
            shaded regions overlap. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
